"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 with a design phase, followed by a development phase led by Omar Jensen. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. A major milestone was reached ahead of schedule with the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype. The executive board approved a $2M budget, with allocations to be discussed in August. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, will be updated starting January next year. Additionally, the team is exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology integration. A separate email mentions a bug report regarding the Zenith system."
